  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting job opportunities in the arts and the peace culture as a means of preventing youth violence in El Salvador.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Asociacin Intersectorial para el Desarrollo Econmico y Progreso Social in El Salvador (CIDEP) works with young people in six municipalities of El Salvador who face high violence rates. CIDEPs methodology not only reaches children and adolescents to give them job and life skills, but also involves and builds supportive local alliances of public authorities and civil society to sustain efforts. It will train young adults in the municipalities of Mejicanos, Ciudad Delgado, Cuscatancingo, Tecoluca, Zacatecoluca and Jiqulisco in leadership, violence prevention, art and culture, and job skills. These young people will form groups and organize community events to promote the culture of peace amidst violent neighborhoods. The grant will benefit 630 people directly and another 4,750 indirectly.</narrative>
  </description>
